  "id": "autonomic-hyperactivity",
  "term": "autonomic hyperactivity",
  "definition": "Autonomic hyperactivity means overactivation of the body's automatic functions, shown by signs such as increased blood pressure, faster heart rate, enlarged pupils, and sweating. In this packet, it is described as a feature seen in alcohol withdrawal delirium.",
